ainst main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring said it used banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That's why the test failed: 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the expected 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed it to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** The request to open the PR timed out, so I checked before trying again to avoid making a duplicate. The PR had been created, but with no reviewers attached, so I added alex to it separately.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system didn't recognise that ID. I followed the test and docstring instead, which both specify banker's rounding. I haven't merged the PR; that needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SoS39ti1C7yR5r7g7fSRxV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Jz1bsYi68pnZ8CEjCUQKFk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VzQHWDc6dmJdGQZiCyi2XX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Git6JFmN9DNGM2FHGrUU9m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ENpKdqKsm4ForHAyrgtGFT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "fr